# FRANK Platform - Environment Configuration
#
# ⚠️  DEPRECATED: This file is deprecated in favor of environment-specific configuration
#
# FRANK now uses environment-centric organization. Configuration files have been
# migrated to the environments/ directory:
#
# Local Development Options:
#
#   1. Docker Compose (recommended for local development)
#      cd environments/local-docker
#      cp .env.example .env
#      vi .env
#      make stage3  # or stage1, stage2
#
#   2. Python Virtualenv (for debugging)
#      cd environments/local-python
#      cp .env.stage3.example .env
#      vi .env
#      ./run-stage3.sh  # or run-stage1.sh, run-stage2.sh
#
# AWS Deployment:
#
#   3. AWS Development
#      cd environments/aws-dev/stage3
#      cp .env.stage3.example .env.stage3
#      vi .env.stage3
#      ansible-playbook ../../ansible/playbook.yml --tags create
#
#   4. AWS Pre-Production
#      cd environments/aws-preprod/stage3
#      cp .env.stage3.example .env.stage3
#      vi .env.stage3
#      ansible-playbook ../../ansible/playbook.yml --tags create
#
#   5. AWS Production
#      cd environments/aws-prod/stage3
#      cp .env.stage3.example .env.stage3
#      vi .env.stage3
#      ansible-playbook ../../ansible/playbook.yml --tags create
#
# For complete documentation, see:
#   - environments/README.md          - Environment overview
#   - environments/local-docker/README.md  - Docker Compose guide
#   - environments/local-python/README.md  - Python virtualenv guide
#   - environments/aws-prod/README.md - AWS deployment guide
